# Cloudflare static-assets headers. Not served itself.
#
# The Stripe Elements iframe is a js.stripe.com document, so its request for our
# font is cross-origin, and a font request is CORS-gated whatever the CDN says.
# Without this the iframe logs "Access to font ... blocked by CORS policy", the
# face reports `status: "error"`, and the card field silently falls back to
# Helvetica beside a page in Archivo. Measured on the PPE worker before and
# after. A public font file is the whole point of serving it, so `*` is the
# accurate answer rather than a list of Stripe hostnames to rot.
/fonts/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
